<title>GERMANY: German Handelsblatt EMU indicator climbs.</title>
<headline>German Handelsblatt EMU indicator climbs.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German daily Handelsblatt's EMU indicator rose to 76 percent from 73 percent as economists said in a poll that agreement on a stability pact at the weekend in Dublin raised the prospects for a stable union.</p>
<p>In a summary of an article to be published in Friday's edition, the newspaper said experts were now even more convinced &quot;that participating nations would remain on course in the run-up to a common currency union.&quot;</p>
<p>More banks also raised their forecast that the currency union would begin as scheduled in January 1999.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
